    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling production of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (79.23). **Gunnar Henderson** holds our premier score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Brown, who carries a shaky 4.53 xERA, while his leadoff spot and strong platoon advantage create the perfect storm for offensive output. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** (72.13) benefit from a soft matchup against Yarbrough, whose 4.76 xERA invites aggressive play. While SB potential remains a primary filter for our roster construction, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) earns a strong start today due to a rare combination of elite speed and a high-leverage leadoff opportunity against Yesavage.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.37), who narrowly missed the cut. While his raw base projection remains high, he faces a stiff challenge in Burke (3.57 xERA), and the optimizer preferred the superior matchup density afforded to **Josh Jung** (60.95) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.06) against more hittable arms. We are managing game caps strictly; consequently, **Brayan Rocchio** (37.26) was an easy exclusion, falling well below our 40-point efficiency floor against the elite Skenes. We remain cautious of **Liam Hicks** (41.90) and **Heliot Ramos** (41.89), whose scores are hovering near the danger zone; if their real-time performance drifts, we will look to rotate in depth pieces like **Coby Mayo** if late-inning pinch-hit opportunities arise to avoid unnecessary cap burn.",
